{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('state.json'))\nq=[i for i in s['investigations'] if i['id'].startswith('533b9664')][0]\nk=[x['id'] for x in s['knowledge'] if x['id'].startswith('533b9664')]\nsrc=['api_verify_doc','raft_verify_leader','repl_notify_all','future_verify_vote','raft_start_stop_repl','raft_quorum_size','raft_leader_lease']\ninterp={\n 'investigation_id':q['id'],\n 'experiment_id':'533b966489544f45b4fcf14f6edce57f-experiment',\n 'source_ids':src,\n 'executions':{'7a54f3754b0b423aaf1ba6c0365367c0':[1,3]},\n 'conclusion':'violated',\n 'defect_claim':'asserted',\n 'rationale':(\\\"Conclusion: violated, and the scoped defect is asserted. VerifyLeader reports success although the leader can reach fewer voters than \\\"\n  \\\"the voter quorum it sized, because acknowledgements arriving on non-voter replication streams are counted as support. Evidence from receipt \\\"\n  \\\"7a54f3754b0b423aaf1ba6c0365367c0 (completed, tests_passed, exit 0). Parsed index 1, the trigger: five members were bootstrapped, two were \\\"\n  \\\"demoted to non-voters, and the leader's transport was disconnected in both directions from the two remaining voters, so voters_reachable=1 \\\"\n  \\\"against quorum_voters=2 while nonvoters_reachable=2; VerifyLeader completed with verify_ok=true and an empty error, and the node was still \\\"\n  \\\"Leader. Parsed index 3, the control on an identically built cluster with the non-voters also disconnected (nonvoters_reachable=0): the same \\\"\n  \\\"call completed with verify_ok=false and the error 'leadership lost while committing log', the node by then a Follower. The two cases differ \\\"\n  \\\"only in whether the non-voters could answer, so the successful verification in the trigger is attributable to non-voter acknowledgements \\\"\n  \\\"rather than to voter support. Mechanism from source: verifyLeader sets quorumSize with quorumSize(), which counts only voters (raft.go:1087-1100), \\\"\n  \\\"but registers the verify future on every entry of leaderState.replState (raft.go:966-990), and startStopReplication creates a replication state \\\"\n  \\\"for every configured server including non-voters (raft.go:583-600); any successful heartbeat or AppendEntries response calls notifyAll(true) \\\"\n  \\\"(replication.go:100-112), which increments the verify future's vote count (future.go:274-293) and completes it at the voter-sized quorum. The \\\"\n  \\\"library already uses the correct supporter set one function away: checkLeaderLease iterates the latest configuration and counts only voters \\\"\n  \\\"(raft.go:1037-1050), so the two paths disagree about who can establish leadership. Consequence under the exercised conditions: a client that \\\"\n  \\\"calls VerifyLeader to protect a read (api.go:927-931) is told the leader still holds a voter quorum while it can reach none of the other voters, \\\"\n  \\\"so the guard against serving stale reads after leadership loss does not hold in a cluster that contains non-voters.\\\"),\n 'counterevidence':[\n  \\\"The verification returned before the lease check stepped the leader down, so the false success is bounded by the leader lease interval rather than permanent; in the control that same step-down produced the error the trigger avoided.\\\",\n  \\\"VerifyLeader returning nil installed no leader and returned no data; the harm requires a client to rely on it as the guard the documentation describes, and this harness issued no reads.\\\",\n  \\\"Non-voter reachability does show the leader is alive and connected, so a deployment that used VerifyLeader only as a liveness probe would not be affected; the code sizes a voter quorum, which makes quorum the stated intent.\\\",\n  \\\"The partition was modelled by removing in-memory transport routing in both directions between the leader and the voters, not by dropping packets or crashing members.\\\"\n ],\n 'limitations':[\n  \\\"One configuration shape was exercised: three voters and two non-voters, with the leader cut from both other voters. Other suffrage mixes, a single non-voter, or a non-voter whose heartbeat is the only one in flight were not tested.\\\",\n  \\\"The exposure window was not measured directly: the harness observed the verification completing immediately after the partition and the leader still in Leader state; how long a false success could persist before the lease check stepped the leader down is bounded by LeaderLeaseTimeout (one second here) but was not sampled.\\\",\n  \\\"No client reads were issued, so the end-to-end stale-read consequence is inferred from the documented purpose of VerifyLeader rather than observed.\\\",\n  \\\"The demotions completed before the partition, but each member's view of the new configuration was not read back before the transport was cut.\\\"\n ],\n 'knowledge':[{'entry_id':k[0],'revision':1,'assertion':'VerifyLeader sizes a voter quorum but registers the verification on every replication stream, including non-voters, whose acks increment its vote count.'},\n              {'entry_id':k[1],'revision':1,'assertion':'checkLeaderLease counts only voters, unlike VerifyLeader.'}]\n}\njson.dump({'rationale':(\\\"Interpret the VerifyLeader execution: with the leader cut from both other voters and the two non-voters reachable, verification \\\"\n  \\\"succeeded against a voter quorum of two; with the non-voters also cut it failed and the leader stepped down. The question is recorded as violated \\\"\n  \\\"with the supporter-set defect asserted, and the lease-bounded window, absent client reads and partition modelling are kept as counterevidence and limits.\\\"),\n 'interpretations':[interp]},open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written', len(interp['counterevidence']), len(interp['limitations']))\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
